SUMMARY:Q & A: Open Government Toolkit for Journalists
DESCRIPTION:Learn about&#160\;The Open Government Toolkit. This toolkit w
 ill be an online resource that provides journalists state-by-state inform
 ation about how to overcome information blockades erected by government a
 gencies and their private contractors. It will answer key questions about
  a wide range of obstructions journalists encounter\, and offer real-time
  advice about how to extract information that by law everyone is entitled
  to obtain.  This project is a partnership between the Reynolds Journalis
 m Institute\, MuckRock and Miranda Spivack.  We would love to show you a 
 prototype to get feedback and ideas for features journalists will need as
  we build it out!  Speakers        Kat Duncan | Director of Innovation\,R
 eynolds Journalism Institute (https://bit.ly/rjiteam)          As Directo
 r of Innovation Kat Duncan leads RJI's innovation team and their initiati
 ves\, programs and workshops.        Miranda Spivack | Independent Journa
 list              Miranda Spivack is a veteran reporter and editor who sp
 ecializes in stories about government accountability and secrecy\, urban 
 development\, and immigration.        Michael Morisy | Chief Executive Of
 ficer\,MuckRock (https://www.muckrock.com/)          Cofounder Michael Mo
 risy is MuckRock's Chief Executive Officer. He's led hundreds of training
 s on transparency\, investigative journalism and civic engagement.
